<title>PHILIPPINES: Anscor, Phinma allowed to raise stakes in bank.</title>
<headline>Anscor, Phinma allowed to raise stakes in bank.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Central Bank has approved the applications of holding concern A. Soriano Corp (Anscor) and the Phinma Group to raise their stakes in AsianBank Corporation to a maximum 60 percent, officials said.</p>
<p>The 60 percent equity ceiling is the maximum permissible stake a Philippine corporation can acquire in a local bank, Central Bank Governor Gabriel Singson said in a statement on Saturday.</p>
<p>Anscor and Phinma each currently control a 39.13 percent stake in AsianBank, a leading investment bank.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8913 Fax 817 6167</p>
